WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.000
Jared Leto has had an interesting career,
to say the least.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.730
He's found massive success as both a singer
and actor, including taking home an Oscar

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.800
for his work in Dallas Buyers Club.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.219
He has sold millions of albums as the frontman
for 30 Seconds to Mars.

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:18.810
He also kind of, maybe, allegedly started
a cult that holds summer camps for devotees.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.810
Allegedly.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.250
Through all of this, Leto has attained a larger-than-life
status, and it's only been bolstered by some

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.050
of the interesting stories about him from
behind the scenes.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.740
Most notably, the actor made headlines while
filming Suicide Squad for getting a little

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.790
too into his role as the Joker.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.440
According to reports from several outlets,
not only did he send a dead pig to his fellow

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.320
cast members, but he also requested everyone
in the cast and crew refer to him as Mistah

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.320
J.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.720
It's safe to say it was method acting taken
to extreme, and it's all the more bizarre

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.320
considering the fact that the Joker doesn't
do anything like sending pigs to anyone in

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.320
Suicide Squad.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.920
Still, it earned the film a ton of publicity,
so it would make sense if he were to carry

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.440
over that technique into a similar role — namely,
that of suspected killer Albert Sparma in

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.620
the neo-noir thriller The Little Things, which
just debuted in theaters and on HBO Max.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.030
Co-star Denzel Washington has said Leto was
on much better behavior during this production.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:10.780
The Little Things stars a trio of Academy
Award winners, with Washington, Leto, and

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.510
Rami Malek all onboard.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.871
The gritty thriller follows two cops from
different California counties who are on the

00:01:15.871 --> 00:01:17.560
hunt for a serial killer.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.780
Leto plays the suspected murderer, and while
this role could have allowed him to let his

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.620
method acting ways come into the picture yet
again, Washington said there were no such

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:27.390
shenanigans in an interview with USA Today.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.120
When the subject of Leto's previous stunts
came up, Washington shut it down, but also

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.040
indicated the bizarre behavior would have
stopped quickly had it appeared.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.040
He said,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.730
"He didn't do any of that with me [...] He'd
have been paid a visit.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.730
That wouldn't happen."

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.090
Apologies to everyone who was hoping for some
on-set fireworks.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.700
On the contrary, Washington seems to have
had a great time working on The Little Things,

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.260
and had nothing but kind things to say about
working with both Leto and Malek.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.260
He said:

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.700
"There's a whole crop of these younger actors,
and it's fascinating to watch them coming

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.790
up behind me [...] Jared is one, obviously,
and Rami is doing great work.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.800
It's inspiring and like a wake-up call.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.720
It's like, I have to get my act together here.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.729
These guys ain't playing."

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:06.240
"You already felt me up, you're armed, I'm
not.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.369
What are you so scared of, little boy?"

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:12.319
Washington doesn't seem to mind passing the
torch, so to speak.

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:15.859
In fact, he even paid to send the late Chadwick
Boseman to the University of Oxford theater

00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:17.000
program in the '90s.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.690
It proved to be an investment very much worth
making.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:23.730
When it comes to adoration for one's co-stars,
it went both ways on the set of The Little

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:24.730
Things.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.530
In an interview with Variety's Awards Circuit
Podcast, Leto revealed he was hesitant to

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.060
join the cast of this movie because he had
already played several characters with similar

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.060
psychology.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.459
But when given the chance to work with this
kind of talent, he just couldn't say no.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:37.459
He said:

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:41.109
"I'm with Denzel Washington and Rami Malek
and [writer-director] John Lee Hancock; I

00:02:41.109 --> 00:02:44.390
thought, 'How can I not be a part of this
incredible opportunity?'

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.029
And I'm really glad that I did.

00:02:46.029 --> 00:02:48.540
Because it was, it was an absolute adventure."

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.730
Leto's certainly no stranger to the industry,
but even seasoned veterans get starstruck

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:57.159
once in a while, and there was plenty of intimidation
to go around on the set of The Little Things.

00:02:57.159 --> 00:02:58.159
Leto explained:

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:01.019
"If he walked in the room, it's still 'Denzel
Washington' to me.

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:02.590
It's not like, 'Hey, what's up Denzel.'

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.669
[...] I just have a lot of respect for him.

00:03:04.669 --> 00:03:06.379
It's not easy to do what he's done.

00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:09.980
And what he's done is he's been great in every
single movie he's ever made."

